cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the SRS/SRT Fractionation Predictor, please cite the software and the publication below."
title: "SRS/SRT Fractionation Predictor: brain-dose, OAR and template prediction for stereotactic radiosurgery and radiotherapy"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-08"
license: MIT
url: "https://ali023273834.github.io/SRS-Frac-Predictor/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ali023273834/SRS-Frac-Predictor"
abstract: "Browser tool that runs a locked model (MATLAB R2025b: Gaussian process regression for brain dose and plan quality, random forest for OAR dose) built on 367 saturated SRS/SRT plans. It predicts normal-brain dose for single-fraction SRS, 27 Gy in 3 and 30 Gy in 5 fractions, recommends the shortest scheme that meets the brain and OAR (TG-101) limits, and retrieves the atlas template to start planning from. Research and validation use only."
